hadiths[22]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1741","Ibrahim ibn Sad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, from Abdullah ibn Jafar who said: I saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eating cucumber with fresh dates."
"1742","Ismail narrated to us, Habib ibn ash-Shahid informed us, from Abdullah ibn Abi Mulaykah who said: Abdullah ibn Jafar said to Ibn az-Zubayr: Do you remember when we met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I and you and Ibn Abbas? He said: Yes. He said: He carried us and left you. And Ismail once said: Do you remember when we met the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, I and you and Ibn Abbas? He said: Yes, and he carried us and left you."
"1743","Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Mawraq al-Ijli, from Abdullah ibn Jafar who said: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came from a journey, he would be met by the boys of his household. He said: He once came from a journey, he said: I was brought forward to him, he said: He carried me before him. He said: Then one of the two sons of Fatimah was brought, either Hasan or Husayn, and he took him behind him. He said: We entered Madinah, three upon a mount."
"1744","Yahya narrated to us, Misar narrated to us, a shaykh from Fahm narrated to me, he said, and I think he is named Muhammad ibn Abdur-Rahman, he said, and I think he is Hijazi, that he heard Abdullah ibn Jafar narrating to Ibn az-Zubayr, and a camel or a large camel had been slaughtered for the people, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, while the people were offering meat to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The best meat is the meat of the back."
"1745","Yazid narrated to us, Mahdi ibn Maymun informed us, from Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abdullah ibn Jafar. Bahz and Affan narrated to us, both saying: Mahdi narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sad, freedman of al-Hasan ibn Ali, from Abdullah ibn Jafar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, took me behind him one day and confided to me a hadith which I shall never inform anyone of. The most beloved covering for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, for his need was a mound or a dense grove of palms. One day he entered a garden of the gardens of the Ansar, and a camel came to him and grumbled and its eyes shed tears. Bahz and Affan said: When it saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, it moaned and its eyes shed tears. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiped its hump and its temples and it calmed. He said: Who is the owner of the camel? A youth of the Ansar came and said: It is mine, O Messenger of Allah. He said: Do you not fear Allah regarding this beast which Allah has made you possess? It has complained to me that you starve it and overwork it."
"1746","Yazid narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah informed us, he said: I saw Ibn Abi Rafi wearing a ring on his right hand, and I asked him about that, and he mentioned that he saw Abdullah ibn Jafar wearing a ring on his right hand, and Abdullah ibn Jafar said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wear a ring on his right hand."
"1747","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Musafi informed me that Musab ibn Shaybah informed him, from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Jafar, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever doubts in his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations while sitting."
"1748","Ishaq ibn Isa and Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, both saying: Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, from Abu al-Aswad who said: I heard Ubayd ibn Umm Kilab narrating from Abdullah ibn Jafar, Yahya ibn Ishaq said: He said: I heard Abdullah ibn Jafar, one of them said: of the two wings, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when he sneezed would praise Allah, and it would be said to him: May Allah have mercy on you, and he would say: May Allah guide you and set right your affairs."
"1749","Nasr ibn Bab narrated to us, from Hajjaj, from Qatadah, from Abdullah ibn Jafar that he said: The last time I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, in one of his hands were fresh dates and in the other cucumber, eating from this and biting from this. And he said: The best of sheep is the meat of the back."
"1750","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub narrating from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abdullah ibn Jafar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent an army and appointed over them Zayd ibn Harithah, and said: If Zayd is killed or martyred, your commander is Jafar; if he is killed or martyred, your commander is Abdullah ibn Rawahah. They met the enemy, and Zayd took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Jafar took the banner and fought until he was killed. Then Abdullah ibn Rawahah took it and fought until he was killed. Then Khalid ibn al-Walid took the banner and Allah granted victory upon him. Their news reached the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he went out to the people, praised Allah and extolled Him, and said: Your brothers met the enemy, and Zayd took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then Jafar ibn Abi Talib took the banner after him and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then Abdullah ibn Rawahah took the banner and fought until he was killed or martyred. Then a sword of the swords of Allah, Khalid ibn al-Walid, took the banner and Allah granted victory upon him. He waited, then gave the family of Jafar three days respite before coming to them, then came to them and said: Do not weep for my brother after today, or tomorrow. Call for me the two sons of my brother. He said: We were brought as if we were young birds. He said: Call the barber for me. The barber was brought and shaved our heads. Then he said: As for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib, and as for Abdullah, he resembles my appearance and character. Then he took my hand and raised it and said: O Allah, succeed Jafar in his family and bless Abdullah in his dealings. He said it three times. He said: Our mother came and mentioned to him our orphanhood and began to express joy to him. He said: Do you fear poverty for them while I am their guardian in this world and the Hereafter."
"1751","Sufyan narrated to us, Jafar ibn Khalid narrated to us, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Jafar who said: When the news of Jafar came when he was killed, the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Prepare food for the family of Jafar, for there has come to them a matter that occupies them, or there has come to them what occupies them."
"1752","Hajjaj narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj informed me, Abdullah ibn Musafi informed me that Musab ibn Shaybah informed him, from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Jafar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever doubts in his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations after he gives salutation."
"1753","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Ibn Jurayj informed us, Abdullah ibn Musafi narrated to us, from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, and he mentioned the like of it with its isnad."
"1754","Wahb ibn Jarir narrated to us, my father narrated to us, he said: I heard Muhammad ibn Abi Yaqub narrating from al-Hasan ibn Sad, from Abdullah ibn Jafar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, rode his mule and took me behind him, and when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, relieved himself, the most beloved place to relieve himself was a mound to screen himself with or a dense grove of palms. He entered a garden of a man of the Ansar, and in it was his working camel. When it saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, it moaned and its eyes shed tears. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, descended and wiped its temples and its hump and it calmed. He said: Who is the lord of this camel? A youth of the Ansar came and said: I am. He said: Do you not fear Allah regarding this beast which Allah has made you possess? It has complained to me of you and claimed that you starve it and overwork it. Then the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, went in the garden and relieved his need, then performed ablution, then came with water dripping from his beard upon his chest. He confided to me something which I shall not narrate to anyone. We urged him to narrate to us and he said: I shall not disclose the secret of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, until I meet Allah."
"1755","Affan narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Rafi, freedman of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that Abdullah ibn Jafar used to wear a ring on his right hand, and claimed that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to wear a ring on his right hand."
"1756","Hashim ibn al-Qasim narrated to us, al-Masudi narrated to us, a shaykh who came to us from Hijaz narrated to us, he said: I witnessed Abdullah ibn az-Zubayr and Abdullah ibn Jafar at Muzdalifah, and Ibn az-Zubayr was cutting meat for Abdullah ibn Jafar. Abdullah ibn Jafar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, saying: The best meat is the meat of the back."
"1757","Ahmad ibn Abdul-Malik narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Ishaq, from Ismail ibn Abi Hakim, from al-Qasim, from Abdullah ibn Jafar who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: It is not fitting for a prophet to say: I am better than Yunus ibn Matta. Abu Abdur-Rahman said: And Harun ibn Maruf narrated it to us likewise."
"1758","Yaqub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq who said: Hisham ibn Urwah ibn az-Zubayr narrated to me, from his father Urwah, from Abdullah ibn Jafar ibn Abi Talib who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: I was commanded to give Khadijah glad tidings of a house of reed in which there is neither noise nor toil."
"1759","Waki narrated to us, Misar narrated to me, from a shaykh from Fahm who said: I heard Abdullah ibn Jafar saying: Meat was brought to the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and the people began to hand him meat. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The best meat is the meat of the back."
"1760","Rawh narrated to us, Ibn Jurayj narrated to us, Jafar ibn Khalid ibn Sarah informed me that his father informed him that Abdullah ibn Jafar said: If you had seen me and Qutham and Ubaydullah, the two sons of Abbas, when we were boys playing, when the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, passed upon a mount and said: Lift this one to me. He said: He carried me before him and said to Qutham: Lift this one to me, and placed him behind him. Ubaydullah was more beloved to Abbas than Qutham, and he was not shy of his uncle that he carried Qutham and left him. He said: Then he wiped over my head three times, and each time he wiped he said: O Allah, succeed Jafar in his offspring. He said: I said to Abdullah: What became of Qutham? He said: He was martyred. He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best the good. He said: Yes."
"1761","Rawh narrated to us, he said: Ibn Jurayj said: Abdullah ibn Musafi informed me that Musab ibn Shaybah informed him, from Uqbah ibn Muhammad ibn al-Harith, from Abdullah ibn Jafar that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever doubts in his prayer, let him prostrate two prostrations after he gives salutation."
"1762","Abdus-Samad narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Rafi, from Abdullah ibn Jafar that he married his daughter to al-Hajjaj ibn Yusuf and said to her: When he comes to you, say: There is no god but Allah, the Forbearing, the Generous; glory be to Allah, Lord of the Mighty Throne; praise be to Allah, Lord of the worlds. And he claimed that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a matter grieved him would say this. Hammad said: I thought he said: And he did not reach her."
